"ff>=0.1.0; extra == \\\\\\\"dev\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"ty==0.0.85; extra == \\\\\\\"dev\\\\\\\"\\\"],\\\"requires_python\\\":\\\">=3.10\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"FLOP Network SDK for Python - HTLC workflows, PoUI proofs, and account management\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"0.2.0\\\",\\\"yanked\\\":false,\\\"yanked_reason\\\":null},\\\"last_serial\\\":42900120,\\\"ownership\\\":{\\\"organization\\\":null,\\\"roles\\\":[{\\\"role\\\":\\\"Owner\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\"}]},\\\"releases\\\":{\\\"0.2.0\\\":[{\\\"comment_text\\\":null,\\\"core-metadata\\\":{\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"f0f5e08fcbfda81ca530f1d29a4d377b2b0dd38f902d6f944da368486aa99dd1\\\"},\\\"digests\\\":{\\\"blake2b_256\\\":\\\"a270de8d4f78263441250f6b98cdf69eda025b50f3bd93be76ca48e8b150533f\\\",\\\"md5\\\":\\\"3eff3599fe4bee1e725fb67a36df5064\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"8951b746cd4f85e33237798b3e3aaf460feb0f870d6ebb6ea2bea3e38b06e5bd\\\"},\\\"downloads\\\":-1,\\\"filename\\\":\\\"flop_sdk-0.2.0-py3-none-any.whl\\\",\\\"has_sig\\\":false,\\\"md5_digest\\\":\\\"3eff3599fe4bee1e725fb67a36df5064\\\",\\\"packagetype\\\":\\\"bdist_wheel\\\",\\\"python_version\\\":\\\"py3\\\",\\\"requires_python\\\":\\\">=3.10\\\",\\\"size\\\":55448,\\\"upload_time\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:27:41\\\",\\\"upload_time_iso_8601\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:27:41.419238Z\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/a2/70/de8d4f78263441250f6b98cdf69eda025b50f3bd93be76ca48e8b150533f/flop_sdk-0.2.0-py3-none-any.whl\\\",\\\"yanked\\\":false,\\\"yanked_reason\\\":null},{\\\"comment_text\\\":null,\\\"core-metadata\\\":false,\\\"digests\\\":{\\\"blake2b_256\\\":\\\"8c0b0dcc701fae9de1a37d13925a08aa3fa90bb429bf6f99df20751602451e47\\\",\\\"md5\\\":\\\"45b4103caa79e146b288cd69322b734b\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"f4466aa6fabf6fdedeb9f3ce82e14e64ddccd52c90b4e836363f6002602b5f5b\\\"},\\\"downloads\\\":-1,\\\"filename\\\":\\\"flop_sdk-0.2.0.tar.gz\\\",\\\"has_sig\\\":false,\\\"md5_digest\\\":\\\"45b4103caa79e146b288cd69322b734b\\\",\\\"packagetype\\\":\\\"sdist\\\",\\\"python_version\\\":\\\"source\\\",\\\"requires_python\\\":\\\">=3.10\\\",\\\"size\\\":66965,\\\"upload_time\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:27:42\\\",\\\"upload_time_iso_8601\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:27:42.641310Z\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/8c/0b/0dcc701fae9de1a37d13925a08aa3fa90bb429bf6f99df20751602451e47/flop_sdk-0.2.0.tar.gz\\\",\\\"yanked\\\":false,\\\"yanked_reason\\\":null}]},\\\"urls\\\":[{\\\"comment_text\\\":null,\\\"core-metadata\\\":{\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"f0f5e08fcbfda81ca530f1d29a4d377b2b0dd38f902d6f944da368486aa99dd1\\\"},\\\"digests\\\":{\\\"blake2b_256\\\":\\\"a270de8d4f78263441250f6b98cdf69eda025b50f3bd93be76ca48e8b150533f\\\",\\\"md5\\\":\\\"3eff3599fe4bee1e725fb67a36df5064\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"8951b746cd4f85e33237798b3e3aaf460feb0f870d6ebb6ea2bea3e38b06e5bd\\\"},\\\"downloads\\\":-1,\\\"filename\\\":\\\"flop_sdk-0.2.0-py3-none-any.whl\\\",\\\"has_sig\\\":false,\\\"md5_digest\\\":\\\"3eff3599fe4bee1e725fb67a36df5064\\\",\\\"packagetype\\\":\\\"bdist_wheel\\\",\\\"python_version\\\":\\\"py3\\\",\\\"requires_python\\\":\\\">=3.10\\\",\\\"size\\\":55448,\\\"upload_time\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:27:41\\\",\\\"upload_time_iso_8601\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:27:41.419238Z\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/a2/70/de8d4f78263441250f6b98cdf69eda025b50f3bd93be76ca48e8b150533f/flop_sdk-0.2.0-py3-none-any.whl\\\",\\\"yanked\\\":false,\\\"yanked_reason\\\":null},{\\\"comment_text\\\":null,\\\"core-metadata\\\":false,\\\"digests\\\":{\\\"blake2b_256\\\":\\\"8c0b0dcc701fae9de1a37d13925a08aa3fa90bb429bf6f99df20751602451e47\\\",\\\"md5\\\":\\\"45b4103caa79e146b288cd69322b734b\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"f4466aa6fabf6fdedeb9f3ce82e14e64ddccd52c90b4e836363f6002602b5f5b\\\"},\\\"downloads\\\":-1,\\\"filename\\\":\\\"flop_sdk-0.2.0.tar.gz\\\",\\\"has_sig\\\":false,\\\"md5_digest\\\":\\\"45b4103caa79e146b288cd69322b734b\\\",\\\"packagetype\\\":\\\"sdist\\\",\\\"python_version\\\":\\\"source\\\",\\\"requires_python\\\":\\\">=3.10\\\",\\\"size\\\":66965,\\\"upload_time\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:27:42\\\",\\\"upload_time_iso_8601\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:27:42.641310Z\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/8c/0b/0dcc701fae9de1a37d13925a08aa3fa90bb429bf6f99df20751602451e47/flop_sdk-0.2.0.tar.gz\\\",\\\"yanked\\\":false,\\\"yanked_reason\\\":null}],\\\"vulnerabilities\\\":[]}\\n\",\"lastModified\":null},{\"source\":\"https://docs.flop.network/docs/sdk-references\",\"status\":200,\"measuredAt\":\"2026-11-06T03:27:33.218Z\",\"body\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\" />\\n<title>SDK and package references \u2014 FLOP docs</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"color-scheme\\\" content=\\\"dark\\\" />\\n<link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"/tokens.css\\\" />\\n<link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"/widget.css\\\" />\\n</head><body><main class=\\\"page hub-page\\\">\\n<a class=\\\"doc__back\\\" href=\\\"/operators?network=devnet\\\">Operator hub</a>\\n<h1 class=\\\"page__title\\\">SDK and package references</h1>\\n<p class=\\\"doc__updated\\\">devnet \u00b7 next \u00b7 development</p>\\n<p class=\\\"doc__updated\\\">Last updated 2026-10-30</p>\\n<article class=\\\"doc__body\\\"><h2>SDK and package references</h2>\\n<p>These are the FLOP packages anyone can install today without a token or a private registry. Each name links to its registry page, which carries the full reference README for the published version. Versions below are the current releases as of 2026-10-30; the registry is authoritative if they differ.</p>\\n<ul><li><a href=\\\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@flop-labs/client\\\">@flop-labs/client</a> <strong>0.2.1</strong> (npm): list models and run chat completions against the public gateway.</li><li><a href=\\\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@flop-labs/contracts\\\">@flop-labs/contracts</a> <strong>0.1.1</strong> (npm): validate public HTTP API payloads with types, JSON Schema and assertions.</li><li><a href=\\\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@flop-labs/sdk\\\">@flop-labs/sdk</a> <strong>0.4.0</strong> (npm): build on the chain from TypeScript, with agent wallets, sessions, HTLCs, PoUI and x402.</li><li><a href=\\\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@flop-labs/pi\\\">@flop-labs/pi</a> <strong>0.3.1</strong> (npm): use FLOP verified inference as a Pi provider, including <code>flop/auto</code> routing.</li><li><a href=\\\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@flop-labs/cli\\\">@flop-labs/cli</a> <strong>0.4.0</strong> (npm): the <code>flop</code> command for keys, networks, miners, validators and models.</li><li><a href=\\\"https://pypi.org/project/flop-sdk/\\\">flop-sdk</a> <strong>0.2.0</strong> (PyPI): build on the chain from Python, with an async client, signed transactions and agent wallets.</li></ul>\\n<p>FLOP has not published Rust crates, a Go module, or the agent SDK, gateway core, x402 types or Hermes plugin packages. A package with one of those names on a public registry is not FLOP's.</p>\\n<h3>Which one do I need?</h3>\\n<ul><li><strong>Call a model from an app or agent:</strong> <code>@flop-labs/client</code>. It speaks the OpenAI-style gateway API and needs only an API key.</li><li><strong>Check gateway responses in your own client:</strong> <code>@flop-labs/contracts</code>.</li><li><strong>Work with accounts, spending limits and settlement on chain:</strong> <code>@flop-labs/sdk</code> (TypeScript) or <code>flop-sdk</code> (Python).</li><li><strong>Use FLOP from the Pi coding agent:</strong> <code>@flop-labs/pi</code>.</li><li><strong>Operate a miner or validator, or script against a network:</strong> <code>@flop-labs/cli</code>. The <a href=\\\"https://docs.flop.network/operators\\\">operator hub</a> has the role manuals.</li></ul>\\n<h3>@flop-labs/client</h3>\\n<p>A small ESM Fetch client for browsers and Node.js 22 or later. Its only runtime dependency is <code>@flop-labs/contracts</code>.</p>\\n<pre><code>npm install @flop-labs/client</code></pre>\\n<pre><code>import { FlopClient } from &quot;@flop-labs/client&quot;;\\n\\nconst client = new FlopClient({ apiKey: process.env.FLOP_API_KEY });\\nconst models = await client.listModels();\\nconst completion = await client.createChatCompletion({\\n  model: models.data[0].id,\\n  messages: [{ role: &quot;user&quot;, content: &quot;Hello&quot; }],\\n});</code></pre>\\n<p>The default base URL is <code>https://api.flop.network/v1</code>. Model discovery needs no key; chat completions do. Methods: <code>listModels</code>, <code>getModel</code>, <code>createChatCompletion</code>, and streaming chat completions. Errors surface as <code>FlopHTTPError</code>. The README also covers caller-owned replay identity, recovering an ambiguous request, and task correlation.</p>\\n<h3>@flop-labs/contracts</h3>\\n<p>Structural types, JSON Schema exports and <code>assert*</code> validators for the public HTTP API: model listing, model lookup, and JSON chat completion requests, responses and stream frames. Node.js 22 or later.</p>\\n<pre><code>npm install @flop-labs/contracts</code></pre>\\n<pre><code>import { assertModelList } from &quot;@flop-labs/contracts&quot;;\\n\\nconst value: unknown = await fetch(&quot;https://api.flop.network/v1/models&quot;).then((r) =&gt; r.json());\\nassertModelList(value);</code></pre>\\n<h3>@flop-labs/sdk</h3>\\n<p>The TypeScript SDK for chain-level work.</p>\\n<pre><code>npm install @flop-labs/sdk</code></pre>\\n<ul><li><code>FlopClient</code>: node health, balances, account info, HTLC creation and status, settlement waits, PoUI submission, compute tasks and TEE quotes.</li><li>Agent wallet functions: <code>createAgentWallet</code>, <code>fundAgentWallet</code>, <code>agentTransfer</code>, <code>ownerWithdraw</code>, <code>createSession</code>, <code>executeViaSession</code>.</li><li><code>x402Fetch</code> and <code>parsePaymentHeaders</code> for HTTP 402 payments.</li><li><code>runDirectSession</code> for a session with a named miner, with identity and receipt checks.</li><li><code>computeChannel.estimateSession</code> and related helpers to size a compute-channel session off chain before opening it.</li><li>Subpath exports: <code>@flop-labs/sdk/react</code> (optional hooks), <code>/browser</code>, <code>/a2a</code>, <code>/ton</code> and <code>/experimental</code>.</li></ul>\\n<p>HTLC creation requires a registered TEE appraisal profile; the README explains the <code>tee_requirements</code> value. <code>SUPPORTED_SPEC_VERSIONS</code> lists the exact runtime versions the SDK admits; both SDKs document theirs in the registry README.</p>\\n<h3>@flop-labs/pi</h3>\\n<p>A <a href=\\\"https://pi.dev\\\">Pi</a> package that adds a <code>flop</code> provider, with one model per offer the gateway lists, and the <code>flop/auto</code> virtual model, which picks a FLOP model for each request. Requires Pi 1.4 or later.</p>\\n<pre><code>pi install npm:@flop-labs/pi</code></pre>\\n<p>Set <code>FLOP_GATEWAY_URL</code> and <code>FLOP_API_KEY</code>. Use a bounded child credential with a spend cap rather than an owner key. Applications that import the <code>/durable</code>, <code>/memory</code> or <code>/memory/paid-storage</code> subpaths install it with <code>npm install @flop-labs/pi</code> instead.</p>\\n<h3>@flop-labs/cli</h3>\\n<p>The <code>flop</code> command. The full CLI needs Node.js 22 or later. Run a pinned release without a global install:</p>\\n<pre><code>npx --yes --package @flop-labs/cli@0.4.0 flop --version</code></pre>\\n<p>A container image, <code>ghcr.io/flop-labs/flop-core/cli</code>, needs only Docker. For a reproducible digest pin, use <a href=\\\"https://flop.network/releases.json\\\">flop.network/releases.json</a>. Commands cover role onboarding, networks and the faucet, health, balances, GPU detection, staking, session keys, named-miner inference, models, gateway configuration, keys and air-gapped signing, and wallets. Add <code>--network &lt;name&gt;</code> to target a network.</p>\\n<h3>flop-sdk (Python)</h3>\\n<p>The Python SDK, for Python 3.10 or later.</p>\\n<pre><code>pip install flop-sdk</code></pre>\\n<pre><code>from flop_sdk import FlopClient\\n\\nasync with FlopClient() as client:\\n    health = await client.health()</code></pre>\\n<ul><li><code>FlopClient</code>: async HTTP client for health, HTLC status and settlement waits.</li><li><code>SubstrateClient</code>: signed transactions such as creating and redeeming HTLCs.</li><li>Wallet functions for agent wallets, funding, transfers, withdrawals and session keys.</li><li>Utilities such as <code>generate_htlc_secrets</code>, amount formatting and address helpers.</li></ul>\\n<h3>Other public surfaces</h3>\\n<ul><li>Public gateway API: <code>https://api.flop.network/v1</code>, the default for <code>@flop-labs/client</code>.</li><li>Hosted read-only MCP server: <code>https://mcp.flop.network/mcp</code> (streamable HTTP).</li><li>The <a href=\\\"https://docs.flop.network/docs/official-links\\\">official links</a> page lists every official domain and account.</li></ul>\\n<p>All of these target the development network today. No FLOP token exists yet, and no package here sells or claims one.</p></article>\\n</main><script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/vce701823e78c4301a35b7e07294d87301792088814092\\\" integrity=\\\"sha512-UKNk8GbxkABxKcXYuLkO16EleLGUkcvJWtpSNmExE0Too3ZaFAxTscNWEc1OdAv5/BikHawapSCaiD2XCmp+Bw==\\\" data-cf-beacon='{\\\"version\\\":\\\"2024.11.0\\\",\\\"token\\\":\\\"98ccdb03ee5f478f8b235d9c5f10bd87\\\",\\\"spa\\\":2}' crossorigin=\\\"anonymous\\\"></script>\\n</body></html>\",\"lastModified\":null},{\"source\":\"https://docs.flop.network/docs/protocol-parameters\",\"status\":200,\"measuredAt\":\"2026-11-06T03:27:33.291Z\",\"body\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\" />\\n<title>Key protocol parameters \u2014 FLOP docs</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"color-scheme\\\" content=\\\"dark\\\" />\\n<link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"/tokens.css\\\" />\\n<link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"/widget.css\\\" />\\n</head><body><main class=\\\"page hub-page\\\">\\n<a class=\\\"doc__back\\\" href=\\\"/operators?network=devnet\\\">Operator hub</a>\\n<h1 class=\\\"page__title\\\">Key protocol parameters</h1>\\n<p class=\\\"doc__updated\\\">devnet \u00b7 next \u00b7 development</p>\\n<p class=\\\"doc__updated\\\">Last updated 2026-10-26</p>\\n<article class=\\\"doc__body\\\"><h2>Key protocol parameters</h2>\\n<p>Every figure below is as stated in the FLOP project intro. Several are explicitly under review; the Status notes say which.</p>\\n<h3>Chain</h3>\\n<div class=\\\"doc__tablewrap\\\"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Block time</td><td>1 s</td><td>Average, with a roadmap toward sub-millisecond settlement</td></tr><tr><td>Block size limit</td><td>2 MB</td><td>Bounds how many proof hashes a block carries</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\\n<h3>Emission</h3>\\n<div class=\\\"doc__tablewrap\\\"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Block reward</td><td>96 FLOP</td><td>Era 0</td></tr><tr><td>Halving period</td><td>730 days</td><td>63,072,000 blocks</td></tr><tr><td>Number of halvings</td><td>5</td><td>Then constant in perpetuity</td></tr><tr><td>Miner share</td><td>75%</td><td>Distributed by verified G_n contribution</td></tr><tr><td>Validator share</td><td>10%</td><td>Shared across the active set</td></tr><tr><td>Agent/broker share</td><td>10%</td><td>Minted to a protocol account; distribution not yet live</td></tr><tr><td>Community-staker share</td><td>5%</td><td>Minted to a protocol account; distribution not yet live</td></tr><tr><td>Era-0 miner pool</td><td>72 FLOP</td><td>Per rewarded block</td></tr><tr><td>Miner pool floor</td><td>2.25 FLOP</td><td>75% of the 3 FLOP floor, after five halvings</td></tr><tr><td>Developer subsidy</td><td>16 FLOP per block</td><td>8 each to FLOP Labs and the FLOP Foundation, on top of the block reward; halves with the reward and stops after five eras, where the reward floors</td></tr><tr><td>Transaction fee burn</td><td>0% (target)</td><td>Ratified zero-burn design; live devnet runtime burns 10% interim (<code>BurnFees</code>) pending runtime upgrade (#2792)</td></tr><tr><td>Audit fee earmark</td><td>1% of session fees</td><td>To validators performing audits; documented, not yet wired</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\\n<h3>Validators</h3>\\n<div class=\\\"doc__tablewrap\\\"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Set size</td><td>1,000</td><td>Capped</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rotation</td><td>~50</td><td>Worst 50 replaced by top 50 in waiting, on uptime and availability</td></tr><tr><td>FIP approval threshold</td><td>2/3</td><td>Of the active set, in most cases</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\\n<h3>Miners</h3>\\n<div class=\\\"doc__tablewrap\\\"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Base self-stake</td><td>10,000 FLOP</td><td>Before the capacity bond</td></tr><tr><td>Capacity bond, nominal</td><td>0.01 FLOP per calibrated GFLOP/s</td><td>Nominal coefficient only</td></tr><tr><td>Capacity bond, live implication</td><td>7,560 FLOP per calibrated GFLOP/s</td><td>After the 604,800-block revocation window and 1.25x surge factor</td></tr><tr><td>Revocation window</td><td>604,800 blocks</td><td>Multiplier on the capacity bond</td></tr><tr><td>Surge factor</td><td>1.25x</td><td>On capacity stake while the cap is burst-ratcheted</td></tr><tr><td>HARD tier capacity cap</td><td>90%</td><td>Of summed governed device ceilings</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\\n<p>&gt; Do not size a miner's stake from the 0.01 coefficient alone. Query the runtime requirement for &gt; the calibrated miner account.</p>\\n<h3>Verification and disputes</h3>\\n<div class=\\\"doc__tablewrap\\\"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Audit rate</td><td>2.5%</td><td>About one session in forty; a governance dial, not a constant</td></tr><tr><td>Challenge window</td><td>~7 days</td><td>Bounded by DA retention; under review to shorten toward hours</td></tr><tr><td>Response deadline</td><td>2 hours</td><td>Silence defaults to a fraud verdict</td></tr><tr><td>Dispute bond</td><td>100 FLOP</td><td>Forfeited if the dispute is frivolous</td></tr><tr><td>Fraud slash</td><td>100%</td><td>Slash, eject, blacklist</td></tr><tr><td>Liveness slash</td><td>1-5%</td><td>Being offline</td></tr><tr><td>TOPLOC commitment size</td><td>258 bytes per 32 tokens</td><td>Retained on the DA layer</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\\n<h3>Distribution</h3>\\n<div class=\\\"doc__tablewrap\\\"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Testnet miner pool</td><td>1,200,000,000 FLOP</td><td>Allocated on verified activity</td></tr><tr><td>Miner airdrop grant</td><td>25% at genesis</td><td>The rest unlocks 1 FLOP per FLOP earned in block rewards and inference fees; no time limit</td></tr><tr><td>Validator airdrop grant</td><td>Locked to the first halving</td><td>Then released one validator per day over 1,000 days</td></tr><tr><td>Agent airdrop release</td><td>1 FLOP per 3 FLOP spent</td><td>Every 3 FLOP of locked airdrop spent on inference unlocks 1 FLOP; the locked balance can be spent only on compute</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\\n<h3>Status</h3>\\n<p>Draft whitepaper and draft design. The capacity-stake constants are under economic reconciliation; the challenge window is under review; transaction-fee routing is interim; the audit-fee earmark is documented but not wired; and the genesis distribution ceremony is not yet wired.</p>\\n<p>The agent/broker and community-staker shares are <strong>minted every block to protocol-held accounts and are not distributed to anyone yet</strong> \u2014 no claim, lock distribution, or rebate path exists for either. Their distribution rules are still being designed.</p></article>\\n</main><script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/vce701823e78c4301a35b7e07294d87301792088814092\\\" integrity=\\\"sha512-UKNk8GbxkABxKcXYuLkO16EleLGUkcvJWtpSNmExE0Too3ZaFAxTscNWEc1OdAv5/BikHawapSCaiD2XCmp+Bw==\\\" data-cf-beacon='{\\\"version\\\":\\\"2024.11.0\\\",\\\"token\\\":\\\"98ccdb03ee5f478f8b235d9c5f10bd87\\\",\\\"spa\\\":2}' crossorigin=\\\"anonymous\\\"></script>\\n</body></html>\",\"lastModified\":null},{\"source\":\"https://docs.flop.network/docs/agent-integration\",\"status\":200,\"measuredAt\":\"2026-11-06T03:27:33.788Z\",\"body\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\" />\\n<title>Integrating an agent with FLOP \u2014 FLOP docs</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"color-scheme\\\" content=\\\"dark\\\" />\\n<link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"/tokens.css\\\" />\\n<link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"/widget.css\\\" />\\n</head><body><main class=\\\"page hub-page\\\">\\n<a class=\\\"doc__back\\\" href=\\\"/operators?network=devnet\\\">Operator hub</a>\\n<h1 class=\\\"page__title\\\">Integrating an agent with FLOP</h1>\\n<p class=\\\"doc__updated\\\">devnet \u00b7 next \u00b7 development</p>\\n<p class=\\\"doc__updated\\\">Last updated 2026-11-03</p>\\n<article class=\\\"doc__body\\\"><h2>Integrating an agent with FLOP</h2>\\n<h3>How does my agent buy inference?</h3>\\n<p>For the executable devnet session path, start with <a href=\\\"https://docs.flop.network/docs/send-to-specific-miner\\\">Send a request to a specific miner</a>. Discover endpoints with <code>flop --network devnet network status</code>; public RPC is <code>wss://rpc.devnet.flop.network</code>, faucet is <code>https://faucet.flop.network</code>, and gateway is <code>https://api.flop.network</code>. Compare faucet <code>/chain</code> with RPC genesis before funding. Faucet <code>/health</code> on older deployments reports signer connectivity, not grant readiness; check indexer lag separately. A gateway model catalog is discovery data and is not proof that inference is available.</p>\\n<p>An expired gateway allowance needs the gateway issuer's supported renewal path; credential rotation or wallet re-enrollment does not renew it. No existing-wallet restoration contact or service deadline is verified in this guide. Follow <a href=\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/network/issues/6\\\">public issue #6</a> for that operator dependency. Keep the same wallet and do not publish bearer credentials.</p>\\n<p><code>flop chat</code> in full CLI <code>0.4.0</code> uses HTLCs, which require a registered EconomicCritical appraisal profile. Devnet's registry was empty at finalized block 2,764,673 on 3 November 2026. That route requires authorized profile registration; neither a flag nor simulator mode supplies it. Direct sessions have their own miner, model, calibration and settlement prerequisites and are not a fallback security claim.</p>\\n<p>Create a <strong>session request</strong> in the mempool. A capable miner accepts, runs the task, and returns a proof. You pay in FLOP on settlement.</p>\\n<h3>What goes in a request?</h3>\\n<p>Five fields:</p>\\n<ul><li>Model-weight hash</li><li>Max latency</li><li>Compute, in FLOPs</li><li>A confidentiality flag</li><li>The fee</li></ul>\\n<h3>What do I get back?</h3>\\n<p>A proof of inference: <strong>activation commitments and a co-signed transcript</strong>. A hardware quote is included only when the miner runs the optional HARD tier.</p>\\n<h3>How do I stop an agent overspending?</h3>\\n<p>The account-based chain carries the controls:</p>\\n<ul><li>Pre-set <strong>spend limits</strong>.</li><li><strong>Delegated bounded authority via proxies</strong>.</li><li><strong>Multisig</strong>, <strong>timelock or vesting</strong>, and <strong>multi-party escrow pools</strong>.</li></ul>\\n<p>See <a href=\\\"https://docs.flop.network/docs/agent-accounts-and-spend-control\\\">agent accounts and spend control</a>.</p>\\n<h3>What if the work is wrong?</h3>\\n<p>Challenge it. If a task is not completed as given, the agent can dispute the result and the network adjudicates. A discretionary challenger posts a <strong>100 FLOP bond</strong>, forfeited if the dispute is frivolous. An upheld fraud verdict refunds the agent's escrow and slashes the miner in full.</p>\\n<h3>Can I hold something other than FLOP?</h3>\\n<p>You can swap. Native hashlock timelocks let an agent escrow FLOP against another chain's asset and exchange it once the counter-transfer confirms \u2014 see <a href=\\\"https://docs.flop.network/docs/atomic-swaps\\\">cross-chain swaps</a>.</p>\\n<h3>Is there an airdrop?</h3>\\n<p>Yes. It arrives locked, and a locked balance can be spent <strong>only on compute</strong>. Every 3 FLOP of it spent on inference unlocks 1 FLOP \u2014 see <a href=\\\"https://docs.flop.network/docs/airdrop-and-testnet-conversion\\\">the airdrop and testnet conversion</a>.</p>\\n<h3>Can my agent earn while idle?</h3>\\n<p>It can lock idle $FLOP in the duration-locked community staking pool to earn a share of the 5% block reward allocation. Operator pools do not support delegated staking.</p>\\n<h3>Status</h3>\\n<p>Draft whitepaper.</p></article>\\n</main><script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/vce701823e78c4301a35b7e07294d87301792088814092\\\" integrity=\\\"sha512-UKNk8GbxkABxKcXYuLkO16EleLGUkcvJWtpSNmExE0Too3ZaFAxTscNWEc1OdAv5/BikHawapSCaiD2XCmp+Bw==\\\" data-cf-beacon='{\\\"version\\\":\\\"2024.11.0\\\",\\\"token\\\":\\\"98ccdb03ee5f478f8b235d9c5f10bd87\\\",\\\"spa\\\":2}' crossorigin=\\\"anonymous\\\"></script>\\n</body></html>\",\"lastModified\":null}],\"gaps\":[],\"requests\":20,\"durationMs\":10444.566705}"
